# Rebuild stock config for an STM32F031 with 16 KB of flash (the x4 part, on
# Recore A3-A6). flash-stm32 reads the chip's flash size register and uses
# this config's build on a 16 KB part, stm32f031-32k's on a 32 KB one.
#
# What the Recore configs use - GPIO (heaters, fans, and servos through
# Klipper's software PWM) and ADC (thermistors, voltage, current) - plus I2C
# (hardware and software) and NeoPixel: 13.6 KB on Klipper v0.13.0-786,
# leaving 2.8 KB for Klipper to grow. Everything else Klipper offers is off.
# Switched on in printer_data/config/firmware/stm32.config, the LDC1612 eddy
# probe (1 KB), buttons and the fan tachometer still fit; the I2C
# accelerometers do not. rebuild-firmware refuses a build over 16 KB.
#
# Until this config the build was 22.7 KB: its =n lines named options Klipper
# had since split up, so they did nothing, and boards ran in flash the part
# is not specified for.
CONFIG_LOW_LEVEL_OPTIONS=y
CONFIG_MACH_STM32=y
CONFIG_MACH_STM32F031=y
CONFIG_STM32_FLASH_START_0000=y
CONFIG_STM32_CLOCK_REF_INTERNAL=y
CONFIG_STM32_SERIAL_USART2_ALT_PA15_PA14=y
CONFIG_WANT_ADC=y
CONFIG_WANT_I2C=y
CONFIG_WANT_NEOPIXEL=y
CONFIG_WANT_BUTTONS=n
CONFIG_WANT_TMCUART=n
CONFIG_WANT_PULSE_COUNTER=n
CONFIG_WANT_ST7920=n
CONFIG_WANT_HD44780=n
CONFIG_WANT_LIS2DW=n
CONFIG_WANT_BMI160=n
CONFIG_WANT_MPU9250=n
CONFIG_WANT_ICM20948=n
CONFIG_WANT_HX71X=n
CONFIG_WANT_CS1237=n
CONFIG_WANT_LDC1612=n
CONFIG_WANT_TRIGGER_ANALOG=n
CONFIG_WANT_STEPPER_OPTIMIZED_BOTH_EDGE=n
